        <detaileddescription>
<para>Gauss-Jordan <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_solver" kindref="compound">Solver</ref></para>
<para>Linear equation solution by Gauss-Jordan elimination, equation (2.1.1) above. The input matrix is a[0..n-1][0..n-1]. b is input containing the m right-hand side. On output, a is replaced by its matrix inverse, and b is replaced by the corresponding solution vector. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>A</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_matrix" kindref="compound">Matrix</ref> A of the linear system Ax=b in nxn </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>b</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the RHS vector b of the linear system Ax=b in n </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
